{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ef0b9450-9790-4b5f-9f7f-0c157f3dd7b5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8413d6f38bd701ec","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-djmm82gc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Manager binary structured reconciliation logging (name/namespace/resourceKind)\n\n## Description\n\nConverts all reconciliation error log calls in the rhods-operator manager binary to the\nstructured logging convention: resource identity emitted as structured key-value pairs\n(`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, camelCase keys) instead of being embedded in message\nstrings. This covers the three diagnosed problems in the manager binary: message-embedded\nresource identity, the DSCInitialization controller's non-standard key names\n(`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and the missing `resourceKind` field across all\ncontroller tiers and action files.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager reconciliation error paths and track coverage\n  in a checklist (grep/static analysis; the audit also confirms the strategy's 75%\n  embedded-identity estimate).\n- Convert every reconciliation error log call that embeds resource name or namespace in the\n  message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n- Migrate the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from the non-standard key names\n  (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs across all five\n  manager controller tiers:\n  - DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller\n  - 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator,\n    Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI)\n  - Module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator)\n  - DSCI controller\n  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n- Update the 15 action files across four tiers to emit `name`, `namespace`, and\n  `resourceKind` on error logs:\n  - 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`)\n  - 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`)\n  - 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`)\n  - 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`)\n- Ensure cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit `name`\n  and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious value.\n- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via test logger output for each\n  controller tier and action file tier.\n- Backwards-compatibility verification: before/after log output comparison for sample\n  reconciliation errors, confirming structured fields appear and the production log consumer\n  stack (Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes; coordinate with\n  SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on the changed message strings and\n  document the required updates.\n- Draft the release-note entry documenting the DSCI key-name migration with before/after\n  query examples (single-release transition).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Static analysis over the manager binary reports zero reconciliation-path `log.Error` calls\n  embedding resource name or namespace in the message string.\n- A codebase grep confirms no remaining use of the `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` field\n  names in DSCI logging, and unit tests assert DSCI error logs contain `name`, `namespace`,\n  and `resourceKind`.\n- Unit tests assert each service controller's (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring,\n  CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error log includes `resourceKind` with the\n  correct value.\n- Unit tests assert error logs in all 15 action files across the four tiers include `name`,\n  `namespace`, and `resourceKind` with correct values.\n- Unit tests assert module controller error logs (including the 8 module handlers) include\n  `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`.\n- Unit tests assert DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include\n  `resourceKind`.\n- Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped resources emit `name` and `resourceKind` and no spurious\n  `namespace` value.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is documented,\n  showing structured fields present and both old and new formats ingested by the production\n  log consumer without configuration changes.\n- Text-based alert rules affected by the changed message strings are identified in\n  coordination with SRE/Support, and the required rule updates are documented.\n- A release note documenting the DSCI key-name migration with before/after query examples is\n  drafted.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: conversion of message-embedded resource identity to structured KV pairs\n  (`name`, `namespace`) — manager binary portion.\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: DSCI controller migration to camelCase key names.\n- **HLR-3 (P0)**: `resourceKind` in service controller error logs.\n- **HLR-4 (P0)**: `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` in all 15 action files across 4 tiers.\n- **HLR-6 (P0)**: `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` in module controller error logs\n  (8 module handlers).\n- **HLR-7 (P1)**: `resourceKind` in DSC and component controller error logs — bundled with the\n  P0 conversion because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites in the same files; a split\n  would double-touch the same files and duplicate the call-site audit.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- **Inconsistent adoption across controllers**: with five controller tiers and 15 action\n  files, some error paths may be missed — mitigated by the grep/static-analysis audit\n  checklist and the CI lint rule that enforces the convention going forward.\n- **Log consumer regression**: existing log-based alerts may match on message strings that\n  change; mitigated by the before/after ingestion verification and SRE/Support alert-rule\n  identification called out in the acceptance criteria.\n- **DSCI query breakage**: operators with existing Loki/CloudWatch queries filtering on\n  `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` are affected; mitigated by the release note and the\n  single-release transition.\n- **Epic size**: per the strategy's effort estimate this epic is ~1.25–1.5 sprints — above the\n  ~2-week guideline. Kept as one logical change: a split would duplicate the call-site audit\n  and fragment a single mechanical conversion. Re-split trigger: re-split this epic if the\n  audit finds materially more `log.Error` call sites than the strategy's 75%-of-calls estimate\n  implies, or if PR-review throughput forces it.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71228,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa16b0116ecc4ba6","agent_id":"ab5882413e4b7889e","session_id":"fa7e0b7e-f01f-43d2-b53c-0d6134573784","uuid":"8ff075da-fc8c-491e-bf41-8dc90cfeae18","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:46:41.739Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
