ge, scope, and suppression guidance are documented.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** (enforcement): the CI lint rule is the durable measurement and\n  regression-prevention mechanism for the structured KV pair conversion — it guards HLR-1\n  through HLR-6 against regression as new code lands. The conversion itself is delivered by\n  the manager-binary and cloudmanager implementation work; this epic delivers only the\n  enforcement tooling (the P0 acceptance criteria allow measurement by one-off static\n  analysis, so enforcement tooling is scheduled as P1).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The rule must be scoped to reconciliation error paths only — the strategy explicitly\n  excludes non-reconciliation log paths (info, debug, warning outside reconciliation error\n  flows) — to avoid false positives blocking unrelated changes.\n- The rule can be developed in parallel with the conversion work: the field convention\n  (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, camelCase) is pinned by the strategy's requirements,\n  so the rule does not wait for the conversion to land.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73763,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa16b0116ecc4ba6","agent_id":"ab5882413e4b7889e","session_id":"fa7e0b7e-f01f-43d2-b53c-0d6134573784","uuid":"53937604-f482-480c-8b5c-77a7d5e125f3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:47:03.312Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
