iteria\n\n- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`,\n  `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n- The guideline includes before/after code examples for the message-embedded-identity\n  conversion and a DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples.\n- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes (manager and\n  cloudmanager binaries) and the review sign-off is recorded.\n- The convention is published in a location accessible to external operator teams, and\n  tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-8 (P1)**: document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- **External adoption is not controllable**: COO team adoption is voluntary per platform\n  policy overlay 0008 — publication and tracking issues are this epic's deliverable; adoption\n  itself is externally controlled and is not an acceptance criterion.\n- **Open product decision**: whether the convention should grow fields beyond\n  name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) is unresolved\n  (PM / Observability team). The guideline documents the three required fields; any extension\n  is follow-up scope.\n- Priority derived from the strategy frontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1) per the\n  docs-authoring priority exception; this epic does not push priority upstream to the\n  implementation work it depends on.\n- Documentation team involvement is listed as \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's\n  prerequisites; the guideline is scoped as engineering documentation owned by the ODH\n  Operator team, with docs-team support to be confirmed at kickoff.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74510,"output_tokens":0},