{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0dbf2883f40917a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: CI lint rule enforcing structured log fields\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: null\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# CI lint rule enforcing structured log fields\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdds a CI lint/static-analysis rule to the rhods-operator repository that flags\n34\treconciliation error log calls (`log.Error` and equivalent error-path logging) missing the\n35\trequired structured fields (`name`, `namespace` where applicable, `resourceKind`), or with\n36\tresource identity embedded in the message string. This makes the structured logging\n37\tconvention durable: it is the measurement mechanism for the conversion acceptance criteria\n38\tand prevents regression as new code lands.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Implement a lint/static-analysis rule that detects:\n43\t  - `log.Error` (and equivalent error-path logging) calls embedding resource name or\n44\t    namespace in the message string;\n45\t  - error-path log calls missing the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace` where\n46\t    applicable, `resourceKind`).\n47\t- Wire the rule into the repository's existing CI pipeline.\n48\t- Document the rule's usage, its scope (reconciliation error paths, per the strategy —\n49\t  info/debug/warning paths outside reconciliation error flows are out of scope), and any\n50\t  suppression/exception mechanism.\n51\t- Validate the rule against fixture examples: a conforming log call passes; a non-conforming\n52\t  call (embedded identity, missing fields) is flagged.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The rule flags a fixture `log.Error` call that embeds resource identity in the message\n57\t  string or omits required structured fields, and passes a fixture call that follows the\n58\t  convention.\n59\t- The rule runs in the repository's CI pipeline, and the pipeline is green with the rule\n60\t  enabled.\n61\t- Rule usage, scope, and suppression guidance are documented.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** (enforcement): the CI lint rule is the durable measurement and\n66\t  regression-prevention mechanism for the structured KV pair conversion — it guards HLR-1\n67\t  through HLR-6 against regression as new code lands. The conversion itself is delivered by\n68\t  the manager-binary and cloudmanager implementation work; this epic delivers only the\n69\t  enforcement tooling (the P0 acceptance criteria allow measurement by one-off static\n70\t  analysis, so enforcement tooling is scheduled as P1).\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- The rule must be scoped to reconciliation error paths only — the strategy explicitly\n75\t  excludes non-reconciliation log paths (info, debug, warning outside reconciliation error\n76\t  flows) — to avoid false positives blocking unrelated changes.\n77\t- The rule can be developed in parallel with the conversion work: the field convention\n78\t  (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, camelCase) is pinned by the strategy's requirements,\n79\t  so the rule does not wait for the conversion to land.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c12a793744784a4","agent_id":"a3cf97bca7c0ca59c","session_id":"fa7e0b7e-f01f-43d2-b53c-0d6134573784","uuid":"78e61771-3153-494e-bf4d-31d9a7202938"