{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a5acddc7570fc20","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E004\n3\ttitle: Structured logging convention contribution guideline\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 4\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Structured logging convention contribution guideline\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tAuthors and publishes the structured logging convention as a contribution guideline for new\n37\tcontroller development in the rhods-operator, and publishes it for voluntary adoption by\n38\texternal operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator: Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) per\n39\tplatform policy overlay 0008. The guideline captures the three-problem diagnosis, the\n40\trequired fields, the naming rationale, before/after code examples, and the DSCI key\n41\tmigration guide.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Author the contribution guideline specifying:\n46\t  - required structured fields: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`;\n47\t  - the camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key\n48\t    conventions);\n49\t  - the three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded identity, DSCI non-standard keys\n50\t    (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), missing `resourceKind`;\n51\t  - before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured\n52\t    key-value pairs;\n53\t  - the DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after query examples;\n54\t  - guidance for new controller development (what every new reconciliation error log must\n55\t    emit).\n56\t- Technically review the guideline against the implemented logging changes in the manager and\n57\t  cloudmanager binaries and against the rhods-operator architecture context, so the documented\n58\t  convention matches what was actually built.\n59\t- Publish the convention in a form accessible to external operator teams and file tracking\n60\t  issues in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`,\n65\t  `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n66\t- The guideline includes before/after code examples for the message-embedded-identity\n67\t  conversion and a DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples.\n68\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes (manager and\n69\t  cloudmanager binaries) and the review sign-off is recorded.\n70\t- The convention is published in a location accessible to external operator teams, and\n71\t  tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-8 (P1)**: document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n76\t  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n77\t\n78\t## Risks / Notes\n79\t\n80\t- **External adoption is not controllable**: COO team adoption is voluntary per platform\n81\t  policy overlay 0008 — publication and tracking issues are this epic's deliverable; adoption\n82\t  itself is externally controlled and is not an acceptance criterion.\n83\t- **Open product decision**: whether the convention should grow fields beyond\n84\t  name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) is unresolved\n85\t  (PM / Observability team). The guideline documents the three required fields; any extension\n86\t  is follow-up scope.\n87\t- Priority derived from the strategy frontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1) per the\n88\t  docs-authoring priority exception; this epic does not push priority upstream to the\n89\t  implementation work it depends on.\n90\t- Documentation team involvement is listed as \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's\n91\t  prerequisites; the guideline is scoped as engineering documentation owned by the ODH\n92\t  Operator team, with docs-team support to be confirmed at kickoff.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c12a793744784a4","agent_id":"a3cf97bca7c0ca59c","session_id":"fa7e0b7e-f01f-43d2-b53c-0d6134573784","uuid":"90152d5b-7e6e-4be9-9fb1-4aa1cb2110e1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:48:55.767Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a5acddc7570fc20","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
