ion, not an artifact of E001/E002, so the\n68\tabsence of an edge is the rule-compliant shape. One minor ambiguity noted in the\n69\tissues list (E003's \"pipeline is green\" AC), which is an AC-clarity matter, not a\n70\tDAG defect.\n71\t\n72\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n73\tComponent/team tuples: E001-E003 are OpenShift AI Productization / ODH Operator\n74\tteam; E004 is Documentation / ODH Operator team — separate epics per the boundary\n75\trule, and both component names are in the canonical list (validator-confirmed).\n76\tNo epic bundles work across teams. E001's above-guideline size (~1.25-1.5 sprints\n77\tper the strategy's own estimate) is a managed trade-off: it is one logical change\n78\t(a single mechanical conversion over one surface), and a concrete re-split trigger\n79\tis recorded both in the summary's Health Warnings and the epic's Risks/Notes —\n80\tcounts as within guideline per the managed-trade-off rule. No scope duplication\n81\tacross siblings: manager vs. cloudmanager are disjoint binaries/controller sets;\n82\tthe lint rule and the guideline are distinct deliverables. No work-product type\n83\tmixing: the release-note draft inside E001 is part of the code-change deliverable,\n84\tnot standalone content authoring; the guideline (content authoring) is correctly\n85\tisolated in E004.\n86\t\n87\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n88\tAll four epics are Implementation, and each produces a concrete artifact (converted\n89\tlog calls + unit tests; cloudmanager conversion; a CI lint rule; a published\n90\tguideline). E004's docs-authoring implementation type is correct per Rule 11. No\n91\tInvestigation epics exist, and the open-question dispositions justify that: none of\n92\tthe four strategy open questions changes which epics exist or what they do (the\n93\t75% audit is the first step of E001's own work; release timing is pure sequencing\n94\tcaptured in E002's risks; the field-extension and alert-inventory questions are\n95\tnon-gating and recorded where relevant). No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact`\n96\tfields are set, consistent with the absence of gates.\n97\t\n98\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n99\tEach Implementation epic carries the 9-signal `ai_signals` field (correct — no\n100\tInvestigation epics exist to require `investigation_signals`), and every\n101\tai-signals rationale file exists with values matching the frontmatter. Signal\n102\tvalues are consistent with the strategy content: E001/E002 score favorable\n103\tchange_specificity/existing_foundation/pattern_precedent on the SME-pinned file\n104\tinventory and confirmed logr foundation; E003 honestly scores pattern_precedent 0\n105\t(no in-repo lint-rule precedent); E004 scores open_questions 0 because the\n106\tunresolved PM field-extension decision touches the guideline's content directly,\n107\twhile E001 scores 1 because no open question changes its code — per-epic judgments,\n108\teach with a coherent rationale. `architecture_claims` calibration is satisfied:\n109\tthe strategy makes architecture claims (controller tiers, action-file counts,\n110\tcloudmanager scope), the rhods-operator architecture-context file exists\n111\t(`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/`), and all four epics\n112\tscore 1 with rationales citing that specific file. E001's\n113\t`human_process_gates: -1` (SRE/Support coordination is part of its verification)\n114\tvs. E002's 0 (its verification is engineering work the team performs, no\n115\tSRE-coordination AC) is a defensible distinction, not a contradiction. Arithmetic\n116\tand thresholds not checked (pipeline-computed).\n117\t\n118\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n119\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy's acceptance criteria\n120\t(static analysis zero-embedded-identity checks, grep for removed DSCI keys,\n121\tunit-test assertions of field presence per tier and per action file,\n122\tcluster-scoped-resource assertions, documented before/after ingestion\n123\tcomparisons, lint fixture pass/fail, guideline review sign-off). Rule-mandated\n124\tACs: E004 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review-against-implementation AC\n125\twith recorded sign-off; no konflux-chain epics exist; the change is additive, not\n126\ta replacement, so rollback/feature-flag ACs do not apply. No AC states an\n127\texternally-controlled precondition: the SRE/Support alert-rule item is\n128\tidentification/coordination work the epic performs (its own deliverable), and COO\n129\tadoption is explicitly kept out of the ACs and in Risks/Notes — the canonical\n130\tsoft-AC trap is correctly avoided. No epic body references sibling epics by\n131\tdraft ID. One minor ambiguity (E003's \"pipeline is green with the rule enabled\")\n132\tis recorded in the issues list.\n133\t\n134\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n135\tEvery strategy capability and acceptance criterion is accounted for: all seven\n136\tstrategy ACs map to epic ACs (embedded-identity conversion, DSCI camelCase\n137\tmigration, service-controller resourceKind, the 15 action files across 4 tiers,\n138\tcloudmanager controllers, cluster-scoped resources, the documented convention).\n139\tThe SME-corrected scope (module controller tier with 8 handlers, 15 action files)\n140\tis fully carried into E001. Strategy-level context is carried forward, not\n141\tdropped: all four risks appear as epic risks and/or health warnings (inconsistent\n142\tadoption → E001 risk + E003 enforcement; log-consumer regression → ACs on E001\n143\tand E002 + health warning; external adoption delay → E004 risk + health warning;\n144\tDSCI query breakage → release-note AC + single-release transition), and all four\n145\topen questions have recorded dispositions. Out-of-scope boundaries are respected\n146\t(E003 explicitly limits the lint rule to reconciliation error paths). The\n147\tbackwards-compatibility NFR is operationalized as ACs on both implementation\n148\tepics; the performance NFR requires no verificatio