{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab3486729c32c72b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Cloudmanager binary structured reconciliation logging\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: null\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Cloudmanager binary structured reconciliation logging\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tApplies the structured logging convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, camelCase\n34\tkeys) to the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary — the companion binary handling multi-cloud\n35\tinfrastructure dependencies on AWS EKS, Azure AKS, and CoreWeave. The three cloudmanager\n36\tcontrollers already receive `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger\n37\tvia the shared reconciler pattern; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource\n38\tidentity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in cloudmanager reconciliation error paths (tracked in a\n43\t  checklist, consistent with the manager-binary audit method).\n44\t- Convert every reconciliation error log call that embeds resource name or namespace in the\n45\t  message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n46\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to the reconciliation error logs of the three\n47\t  cloudmanager controllers: AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n48\t  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine.\n49\t- Ensure cluster-scoped infrastructure resources emit `name` and `resourceKind` with\n50\t  `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious value.\n51\t- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via test logger output for each of\n52\t  the three controllers.\n53\t- Backwards-compatibility verification for cloud environments: before/after log output\n54\t  comparison for sample reconciliation errors, confirming the cloud log consumers (e.g.,\n55\t  CloudWatch on EKS/AKS) ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Static analysis over the cloudmanager binary reports zero reconciliation-path `log.Error`\n60\t  calls embedding resource name or namespace in the message string.\n61\t- Unit tests assert the reconciliation error logs of all three cloudmanager controllers\n62\t  (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) include `name`,\n63\t  `namespace`, and `resourceKind` with correct values.\n64\t- Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped infrastructure resources emit `name` and `resourceKind`\n65\t  and no spurious `namespace` value.\n66\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is documented,\n67\t  showing structured fields present and both old and new formats ingested by the cloud log\n68\t  consumer without configuration changes.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: conversion of message-embedded resource identity to structured KV pairs —\n73\t  cloudmanager binary portion.\n74\t- **HLR-5 (P0)**: `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` in all cloudmanager controller\n75\t  reconciliation error logs.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- **Release timing**: whether this work ships in the same release as the manager-binary\n80\t  conversion or a subsequent one is an open product decision. This epic is independent of the\n81\t  manager-binary work and has no downstream dependents besides the convention guideline, so\n82\t  either sequencing works without restructuring.\n83\t- **Narrower impact scope**: cloudmanager is only deployed on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS\n84\t  EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so the log-consumer regression surface (CloudWatch rather than\n85\t  Loki) is narrower than the manager binary's.\n86\t- Per the strategy's effort estimate this epic is ~0.25 sprint — well within the epic-size\n87\t  guideline.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7a6b45285b9a171","agent_id":"a65b604becdab9c7c","session_id":"fa7e0b7e-f01f-43d2-b53c-0d6134573784","uuid":"ca85d5b8-93c2-4d34-8af6-00301b916974","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:53:09.894Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab3486729c32c72b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
